# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Docker compose data dir
.docker

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# user-customized env file
.env

# compiled program
ocf-ims
compose.ocf-ims

node_modules

# the default dir for storing attachments
ims-attachments

# the temp dir for `go tool air`
air_tmp

# Generated code — NOT committed. All of it is produced at build time by
# `go run bin/build/build.go` (use `-generate-only` to skip the final compile),
# and also in the Docker build + CI. One convention: no generated code in the tree.
# The Go tree lives under go/ (plan 09f); the proto TS target stays with the
# repo-root pnpm workspace.
#   sqlc  -> go/store/imsdb/, go/directory/clubhousedb/
#   templ -> go/web/template/*_templ.go
#   tsgo  -> go/web/static/*.js
#   buf   -> go/gen/ (Go + connect-go + OpenAPI), packages/protocol-buffers/src/ (TS)
/go/store/imsdb/
/go/directory/clubhousedb/
/go/web/template/*_templ.go
/go/web/static/*.js
/go/gen/
/packages/protocol-buffers/src/

# session/tool artifacts
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.playwright-mcp/

# local editor workspace config (Obsidian, for reading docs/plans as a vault)
.obsidian/

# local monitoring config (log viewer + localhost compose override)
docker-compose.monitoring.localhost.yml
dozzle-users.yml
